#!/bin/sh
# Wingbox plugin launcher for Claude Code: runs `wingbox <arguments>`.
# 1. the installed wingbox command (pipx install wingbox);
# 2. otherwise uvx from the release commit pinned below (the newest vX.Y.Z tag;
#    tools/sync_plugin.py keeps it current; written literally in both lines because
#    the plugin directory reads the pin from the command text); the first run fetches it from GitHub;
# 3. otherwise a message that names pipx install wingbox, exit 127.
# The search hook (first argument "hook") never blocks a tool call: it is
# silent and exits 0 when wingbox is missing or fails, and it uses uvx only
# offline, from the uv cache.
if [ "$1" = "hook" ]; then
  if command -v wingbox >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    wingbox "$@" 2>/dev/null
  elif command -v uvx >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    uvx --offline --quiet --from git+https://github.com/aileron-tech/wingbox@8481a35b08c3078d8f898c52dd5f679206bbdd2d wingbox "$@" 2>/dev/null
  fi
  exit 0
fi
if command -v wingbox >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  exec wingbox "$@"
fi
if command -v uvx >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  exec uvx --quiet --from git+https://github.com/aileron-tech/wingbox@8481a35b08c3078d8f898c52dd5f679206bbdd2d wingbox "$@"
fi
echo "wingbox: the wingbox command is not installed. Install it with: pipx install wingbox" >&2
echo "(or install uv from https://docs.astral.sh/uv/ and the plugin runs wingbox through uvx)" >&2
exit 127
